Somebody (Sorry!  I forgot your name.) recently posted a patch to display
your kill list after you die.  I put it in my version, and it's really
fun.  It's a great idea.

As a matter of personal taste, I wanted to order the list of kills in 
ascending ferocity.  A bone-headed, but very simple way to do that is
as follows:

at:

>kill_list()
>{
>  char buf[BUFSZ];
>  int i, nk;

replace the last line with:

+  int i, l, nk;

and replace:

>  for (i=0; i < NUMMONS; i++)  {
>    if (((nk = u.nr_killed[i]) > 0) || (mons[i].geno & G_GENOD))  {

with:

+ for (l=0; l<=106; l++) {	/* Demogorgon = level 106 */
+  for (i=0; i < NUMMONS; i++)  {
+   if ((mons[i].mlevel == l) && (((nk = u.nr_killed[i]) > 0) || (mons[i].geno & G_GENOD)))  {

and add one more } right above:

>  cornline(2, "");

at the end of the function...

